<title>INDIA: FOCUS - Delhi Stock Exchange to recast index.</title>
<headline>FOCUS - Delhi Stock Exchange to recast index.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Delhi Stock Exchange (DSE) will replace 18 existing shares with more actively-traded stocks in a major recast of its 33-share benchmark index introduced in 1983, stock exchange officials said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The DSE said in a statement the new index, which would come into effect from Monday, will include 18 new scrips in addition to 15 which have been retained in the recast.</p>
<p>Subhash Chugh, vice-president of the Delhi Stock Exchange said market capitalisation, industry performance and turnover on the exchange were the main criteria for the selection of the new entrants to the index weightage list.</p>
<p>Consumer goods giant Hindustan Lever Ltd will have the maximum weightage in the new index, the statement said.</p>
<p>Following are the 18 new shares in the index:</p>
<p>BSES Ltd</p>
<p>Chambal Fertiliser and Chemicals</p>
<p>DCM Daewoo Motors</p>
<p>Essar Shipping</p>
<p>Essar Steel</p>
<p>Hindalco Industries</p>
<p>ICICI</p>
<p>IPCL</p>
<p>Indo Gulf Fertilisers and Chemicals</p>
<p>IFCI Ltd</p>
<p>ITC Ltd</p>
<p>Jaiprakash Industries</p>
<p>Larsen and Toubro</p>
<p>MTNL</p>
<p>Oriental Bank of Commerce</p>
<p>Oswal Chemicals and Fertilisers</p>
<p>State Bank of India</p>
<p>Steel Authority of India</p>
<p>The new index would represent the following major industry segments:</p>
<p>Cement, tyres, hotels, power, fertiliser, real estate, light commercial vehicles/cars, engineering, shipping, construction, textiles, scooters, telecommunications, food, banking, pharmaceuticals, heavy vehicles, sugar, steel, motorcycles, aluminium, tea, personal care, financial services, petrochemicals and cigarettes.</p>
<p>The following shares have been excluded from the new index:</p>
<p>DCM Shriram industries Ltd</p>
<p>E.I. Hotels</p>
<p>Grasim Industries</p>
<p>Gujarat Narmada Valley Fertilisers</p>
<p>Hindustan Motor</p>
<p>J.K. Industries</p>
<p>J.K. Synthetics</p>
<p>Modi Industries</p>
<p>Modi Rubber</p>
<p>Orkay Industries</p>
<p>Oswal Agro Mills</p>
<p>Prakash Industries</p>
<p>Rig Transmission</p>
<p>SIEL</p>
<p>Smithkline Beecham Consumer Healthcare</p>
<p>SPIC</p>
<p>SRF Ltd</p>
<p>Swadeshi Polytex</p>
<p>The following scrips have been retained:</p>
<p>ACC, Apollo Tyres, Asian Hotels, DCM Ltd, DCM Shriram Consolidated, Escorts, Hero Honda, Hindustan Lever, JCT, LML Ltd, Nestle India, Ranbaxy, Reliance Industries, TELCO and TISCO.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
